  The caption says the father-in-law was found lying inside the house 'after' drinking and then 'received treatment at a private hospital' - the article says the son-in-law left while he was unconscious, which is consistent, but the caption's 'வீட்டிற்குள் மயங்கிக் கிடந்தார்' is fine; however the caption's phrase 'நேற்று முன்தினம் உயிரிழந்தார்' is placed directly after treatment without the article's 'சிகிச்சை பலனளிக்காமல்' context, which is acceptable.
  The caption's claim that the injury was from falling 'போதையில் கீழே விழுந்ததில்' is stated as the son-in-law's account in the article, but the caption and reel script present a cause mixed with the arrest without noting it is only the accused's statement in the caption's summary line; the caption says 'போலீசாரிடம் கூறியுள்ளார்' so this is attributed - no problem here.
